{"toolCallId":"call_0799b9de93064c7d84b31776aa132686","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/224-deepseek-final2/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n<!-- FILL: Fill the stack row and write three sentences: what changes, where, and how you will prove it. GOOD: Change one bash script. Add one output branch. Prove it with a line count. WEAK: This plan describes the implementation. -->\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., TypeScript, Python 3.11] |\n| **Framework** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., React, FastAPI] |\n| **Storage** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., PostgreSQL, None] |\n| **Testing** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., Jest, pytest] |\n\n### Overview\n[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n<!-- FILL: Turn each gate into a check a command can answer. Keep the boxes unticked until they pass. GOOD: `rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh` prints the new branch before the task starts. WEAK: The team agrees the plan is ready. -->\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n<!-- FILL: Name the pattern in three words, then list the one component that changes. GOOD: Single script branch. The component is `recommend-level.sh`. WEAK: Standard architecture. -->\n\n### Pattern\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: MVC | MVVM | Clean Architecture | Serverless | Monolith | Other]\n\n### Key Components\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 1]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 2]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n\n### Data Flow\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description of how data moves through the system]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n<!-- FILL: Name each surface the change touches. Write `not a consumer` when it does not read the change. Write `N/A` or delete the whole addendum when no fix surface applies. GOOD: `recommend-level.sh`: owns the output. Action: update. WEAK: Various files. -->\n\nUse this section when `research_intent=fix_bug`, when planning from a deep-review FAIL/CONDITIONAL verdict, or when any finding touches security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence, public responses, or shared policy.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: producer/helper/policy] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: what owns the behavior] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: grep/test/doc evidence] |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: consumer/status/docs/tests] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: how it observes the behavior] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: grep/test/doc evidence] |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n '<field|string|helper|literal|error-pattern>' <module-or-files>`.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `rg -n '<changedSymbol>|<changedConstant>|<changedPublicField>' . --glob '*.ts' --glob '*.js' --glob '*.md'`.\n- Matrix axes: list every independent input axis and the required rows before implementation.\n- Algorithm invariant: for path/redaction/parser/resolver/security fixes, state the invariant and adversarial cases.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n<!-- FILL: Point to `tasks.md` and name the three phases in one line. GOOD: Setup reads the current output. Implementation adds the branch. Verification counts lines. WEAK: See tasks. -->\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n<!-- FILL: Name the one command you will run and the output it must print. GOOD: `--quiet` prints 1 line. The default prints 17. WEAK: Test it manually. -->\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Components/functions] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Jest/pytest/etc.] |\n| Integration | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: API endpoints/flows] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Tools] |\n| Manual | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: User journeys] | Browser |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: List each tool the change needs, or write `None`. GOOD: `bash` and `awk`. No new package. WEAK: Usual dependencies. -->\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: System/Library] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Internal/External] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Green/Yellow/Red] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Impact] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger and the one command that reverts the change. GOOD: Trigger: the default output changes. Revert the one commit. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\n- **Trigger**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Conditions requiring rollback]\n- **Procedure**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How to revert changes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: Draw the phase order in the fence, then fill the table with depends-on and blocks. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Setup to Implementation to Verification. Verification blocks close. WEAK: Phases depend on each other. -->\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──────┐\n                      ├──► Phase 2 (Core) ──► Phase 3 (Verify)\nPhase 1.5 (Config) ───┘\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Core, Config |\n| Config | Setup | Core |\n| Core | Setup, Config | Verify |\n| Verify | Core | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n<!-- FILL: Give each phase an estimate and a total. Mark the total as an assumption. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Setup 10 minutes, implementation 30, verification 10. Total 50 minutes. WEAK: A few hours. -->\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| Core Implementation | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 4-8 hours] |\n| Verification | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| **Total** | | **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 6-12 hours]** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger, the steps and the data reversal. Write `No` when no data changes. Delete the whole section when the packet ships no deployable service. GOOD: Trigger: default output changes. Steps: revert one commit, rerun the two commands. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Backup created (if data changes)\n- [ ] Feature flag configured\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Immediate action - e.g., disable feature flag]\n2. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Revert code - e.g., git revert or redeploy previous version]\n3. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Verify rollback - e.g., smoke test critical paths]\n4. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Notify stakeholders - if user-facing]\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Yes/No]\n- **Reversal procedure**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Steps or \"N/A\"]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n<!-- FILL: Draw the component order and fill the matrix with produces and blocks. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Script to test to close. WEAK: Components depend on each other. -->\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘     └─────────────┘\n                          │\n                    ┌─────▼─────┐\n                    │  Phase 2b │\n                    │  Parallel │\n                    └───────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component A] | None | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | B, C |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component B] | A | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | D |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component C] | A | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | D |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component D] | B, C | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Final] | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n<!-- FILL: Name the longest chain and its total. List what can run in parallel. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Implementation to verification, 40 minutes. Docs run in parallel. WEAK: The critical path is the main path. -->\n\n1. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n2. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n3. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Sum of durations]\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task A] and [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task B] can run simultaneously\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task C] and [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task D] can run after Phase 1\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n<!-- FILL: Name three milestones with a command-checkable success criterion. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: M1: the branch exists. `rg -n quiet` prints it. WEAK: Milestones are tracked. -->\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Setup Complete] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: All dependencies ready] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n| M2 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Core Done] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Main features working] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n| M3 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Release Ready] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: All tests pass] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n<!-- FILL: Write one ADR per decision. Name the context, the choice, the consequence and the rejected option. GOOD: ADR-001: a flag, because callers already pass flags. WEAK: We made a decision. -->\n\n### ADR-001: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Decision Title]\n\n**Status**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Proposed/Accepted/Deprecated]\n\n**Context**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What problem we're solving]\n\n**Decision**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What we decided]\n\n**Consequences**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Positive outcome 1]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Negative outcome + mitigation]\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Option B]: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Why rejected]\n\n---\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add a --quiet branch to the existing argument parser and a renderer that prints only the Recommended Level line. The default report, JSON output, scoring and exit codes stay unchanged, and a vitest case pins both outputs.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2 or newer, the version macOS ships |\n| **Framework** | None. A standalone script with `set -euo pipefail` |\n| **Storage** | None |\n| **Testing** | vitest in the `runtime/cli` workspace, plus direct shell runs |\n\n### Overview\nChange one script. The argument parser gets a `--quiet` branch that sets a global, and the output dispatch gets a third renderer that prints only `Recommended Level: N (Name)`. A new vitest case runs the script with and without the flag and asserts the line count and the exact bytes of the default report.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [x] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [x] Success criteria measurable\n- [x] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] `npx vitest run tests/recommend-level-quiet.vitest.ts` passes\n- [ ] `node tests/test-phase-system.js` and `node tests/test-phase-validation.js` still pass\n- [ ] `bash -n recommend-level.sh` exits 0\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nSingle-script flag branch.\n\n### Key Components\n- **Argument parser**: the `while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; case \"$1\"` loop at lines 656-719 of `recommend-level.sh`. It already handles `--json|-j`, `--no-recommend-phases` and `--phase-threshold`.\n- **Renderers**: `output_text` at lines 508-558 and `output_json` at lines 562-649. Each reads the scored globals and writes to stdout.\n- **Output dispatch**: lines 770-774 choose a renderer from `JSON_OUTPUT`. The quiet branch joins this decision point.\n\n### Data Flow\nArguments set globals, the scoring functions fill `TOTAL_SCORE`, `determine_level` sets `RECOMMENDED_LEVEL` and `LEVEL_NAME`, and one renderer prints. `--quiet` changes only the renderer choice. Scoring, confidence and phase calculation run exactly as they do today.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| `recommend-level.sh` argument parser | Owns option handling | Update | `rg -n -- '--quiet' recommend-level.sh` shows the case branch |\n| `output_text` level line | Producer of `Recommended Level: N (Name)` | Unchanged | Test asserts the default report is byte-identical |\n| New quiet renderer | Producer of the one-line answer | Create | `--quiet \\| wc -l` prints 1 |\n| `output_json` | Producer for machine callers | Unchanged | Test asserts `--json --quiet` parses as JSON |\n| `--help` text and header OPTIONS | Documentation surface | Update | `--help \\| rg -c -- '--quiet'` prints 2 |\n| `tests/test-phase-system.js`, `tests/test-phase-validation.js` | Consumers that run the script | Not a consumer of the flag; regression only | Both still pass |\n| Other shell callers | None found | Not a consumer | `rg -n \"recommend-level\\.sh\" --glob '*.sh'` returns only the script itself |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n 'Recommended Level' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` returns the header comment, the `output_text` line and the help text. Only `output_text` emits the line at runtime, so the quiet renderer reuses that string.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `rg -n 'recommend-level\\.sh' . --glob '*.sh' --glob '*.js' --glob '*.ts' --glob '!node_modules/**' --glob '!specs/**'` returns the script and two test files. No shell caller parses the report.\n- Matrix axes: flag combination (none, `--quiet`, `--json`, both) by phase mode (default, `--no-recommend-phases`) by input validity (valid, missing numbers, non-numeric, unknown option). Twelve rows, four of them covered by the new test and the rest by the verification tasks.\n- Algorithm invariant: the quiet line equals the first content line of the default report, with the leading blank line removed. The invariant breaks if either renderer builds its own label, so both read `RECOMMENDED_LEVEL` and `LEVEL_NAME` through one shared string.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state. Setup captures the pre-change output. Implementation adds the parser branch, the renderer and the help text. Verification runs the new test, the two existing phase tests and the line counts.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | Quiet renderer output and the shared label string | vitest, `execFileSync('bash', ...)` |\n| Integration | Flag combinations: none, `--quiet`, `--json`, both, with and without `--no-recommend-phases` | vitest |\n| Regression | Default report bytes for the `--help` examples | vitest snapshot comparison against the captured baseline |\n| Manual | `--help`, missing input, non-numeric input, unknown option | shell |\n\nThe new test lives at `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/recommend-level-quiet.vitest.ts`. The CLI vitest project includes `tests/**/*.vitest.ts`, so no config change is needed.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| `bash` 3.2+ | Internal | Green | The script cannot run |\n| `vitest` 4.x in the `runtime/cli` workspace | Internal | Green | Tests fall back to direct shell checks |\n| `node` 22.12+ | Internal | Green | The existing test suites cannot run |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n- **Trigger**: The default report changes for any `--help` example, or a phase test fails after the change.\n- **Procedure**: Revert the single commit that touches `recommend-level.sh` and the new test file. Confirm `recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2 | wc -l` prints 16 again.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n## AI Execution Protocol\n\n### Pre-Task Checklist\n\nBefore starting a task:\n\n1. Read `spec.md` and confirm the requested work stays inside section 3.\n2. Read this plan and identify the phase the task belongs to.\n3. Read `tasks.md` and pick the next incomplete task.\n4. Capture the current output of the command the task changes, so the comparison has a baseline.\n5. Confirm the write path is the script or the new test file, nothing else.\n\n### Execution Rules\n\n| Rule | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| TASK-SEQ | Capture the baseline before editing, then parser, then renderer, then test |\n| TASK-SCOPE | Touch only `recommend-level.sh` and the new test file |\n| TASK-VERIFY | Run each task's `Verify:` command and read its output before marking the task done |\n| TASK-DOC | Reconcile spec, plan and tasks only after the checks pass |\n\n### Status Reporting Format\n\nReport `Task`, `Status`, `Evidence`, `Blockers` and `Next` after each task.\n\n### Blocked Task Protocol\n\nIf a task is blocked, stop dependent work, record the failing command and its output, keep the task open, and state the decision needed to continue.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──────┐\n                      ├──► Phase 2 (Core) ──► Phase 3 (Verify)\nPhase 1.5 (Test scaffold) ─┘\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Core, Test scaffold |\n| Test scaffold | Setup | Verify |\n| Core | Setup | Verify |\n| Verify | Core, Test scaffold | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | Low | 10 minutes |\n| Core Implementation | Low | 30 minutes |\n| Verification | Low | 20 minutes |\n| **Total** | | **About 1 hour** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [x] Backup created (not applicable; the change is one tracked file under version control)\n- [ ] Feature flag configured (not applicable; `--quiet` is the opt-in itself)\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set (not applicable; the script is not a service)\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. Revert the commit that touches `recommend-level.sh` and the new test file.\n2. Run `bash recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2 | wc -l` and confirm 16.\n3. Run the two phase test files and confirm both pass.\n4. Tell callers that used `--quiet` that the flag is gone.\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** No\n- **Reversal procedure**: N/A. The script stores no state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Baseline  │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘     └─────────────┘\n                          │\n                    ┌─────▼─────┐\n                    │  Test     │\n                    │  scaffold │\n                    └───────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| Baseline capture | None | 16-line and 17-line reference output | Quiet renderer test |\n| Parser branch | None | `QUIET` global set from `--quiet` | Renderer dispatch |\n| Quiet renderer | Parser branch | One-line stdout | Test |\n| Help text | Parser branch | Documented flag | Docs verification |\n| Test case | Baseline, renderer, help | Regression proof | Close |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n\n1. **Baseline capture** - 5 minutes - CRITICAL\n2. **Parser branch and quiet renderer** - 20 minutes - CRITICAL\n3. **Test case and full run** - 15 minutes - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: About 40 minutes\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- The help text and the header OPTIONS block can be edited with the parser branch.\n- The test file can be scaffolded while the renderer lands, because the baseline capture already fixed the expected bytes.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | Flag parsed | `rg -n -- '--quiet' recommend-level.sh` shows the case branch | Phase 2 start |\n| M2 | One line printed | `recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet \\| wc -l` prints 1 | Phase 2 end |\n| M3 | Proof in place | New vitest passes and both phase test files still pass | Phase 3 end |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n### ADR-001: A flag rather than an environment variable or a new format\n\n**Status**: Proposed\n\n**Context**: A caller needs the level without the report. The script already takes options, and `--json` returns a whole object.\n\n**Decision**: Add `--quiet` to the existing parser. It sets a global and selects a renderer.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- The caller opts in per invocation, so no state leaks between runs.\n- One more option to document and test.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Environment variable `SPECKIT_QUIET`: hidden from `--help`, easy to inherit into unrelated runs.\n- `--json` piped to a JSON parser: adds a parser dependency and returns more than the caller asked for.\n- A new `--format level` option: new vocabulary for a single use.\n\n---\n\n### ADR-002: JSON wins when both `--json` and `--quiet` appear\n\n**Status**: Proposed\n\n**Context**: A shared argument builder can pass both machine-oriented flags.\n\n**Decision**: `--json` takes precedence. The quiet renderer only replaces the human report.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- One documented rule: `--quiet` affects text output.\n- A caller that asks for JSON still receives parseable JSON.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Quiet wins: a JSON request would return a text line, which is surprising and harder to detect.\n- Reject the pair with exit 1: breaks argument builders that always append `--quiet`; adds a failure path for no gain.\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":129,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":85}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/224-deepseek-final2/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
