{"toolCallId":"call_94cdb85f098949daa0a6a28ef76bbbe4","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/224-deepseek-final2/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Paths used below**:\n- `S` = `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`\n- `T` = `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/recommend-level-quiet.vitest.ts`\n- `P` = `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Capture the pre-change report for both reference invocations into `$P/scratch/baseline-report.txt` (`$P/scratch`). Verify: `bash $S --loc 50 --files 2 | wc -l` prints `16` and `bash $S --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural | wc -l` prints `17`.\n- [ ] T002 Read the parser and the output dispatch in `$S`. Verify: `rg -n 'JSON_OUTPUT|output_text|output_json' $S` prints the three decision sites at lines 122, 508, 562 and 770-774.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm no shell consumer parses the report (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'recommend-level\\.sh' . --glob '*.sh' --glob '!node_modules/**'` prints only the script itself.\n- [ ] T004 [P] Record the level label set (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'LEVEL_NAME=' $S` prints `Quick`, `Baseline`, `Verification` and `Full`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T005 Add a `QUIET=false` global beside `JSON_OUTPUT` (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '^QUIET=false' $S` prints one line.\n- [ ] T006 Add the `--quiet` case branch to the argument parser (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n -A 3 -- '--quiet\\)' $S` prints the branch that sets `QUIET=true` and shifts.\n- [ ] T007 Add `output_quiet()` that prints only `Recommended Level: ${RECOMMENDED_LEVEL} (${LEVEL_NAME})` (`$S`). Verify: `bash -n $S` exits 0.\n- [ ] T008 Wire the dispatch so `--quiet` selects the quiet renderer, `--json` keeps precedence and text stays the default (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet | wc -l` prints `1`; `bash $S --loc 50 --files 2 | wc -l` still prints `16`.\n- [ ] T009 Add `--quiet` to the `--help` OPTIONS list and add one quiet example, then update the header OPTIONS block (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --help | rg -c -- '--quiet'` prints `2`.\n- [ ] T010 [P] Create the regression test with cases for none, `--quiet`, `--json`, both flags, `--no-recommend-phases`, and the error paths (`T`). Verify: `npx vitest run tests/recommend-level-quiet.vitest.ts` passes from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T011 Verify the quiet line at every level: 0, 1, 2 and 3 (`$S`). Verify: each of `--loc 10 --files 1`, `--loc 100 --files 5`, `--loc 300 --files 10`, `--loc 900 --files 20 --auth --api --db --architectural` with `--quiet` prints one line that matches `^Recommended Level: [0-3] \\([A-Za-z]+\\)$`.\n- [ ] T012 Verify the default report is byte-identical to the Phase 1 baseline (`$P/scratch`). Verify: `diff` against `baseline-report.txt` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T013 Verify JSON precedence (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --loc 50 --files 2 --json --quiet | node -e 'let s=\"\";process.stdin.on(\"data\",d=>s+=d).on(\"end\",()=>{const j=JSON.parse(s);console.log(j.recommended_level)})'` prints `0`.\n- [ ] T014 Verify error paths keep stdout empty and exit 1 (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet --loc abc` prints the error on stderr, writes nothing to stdout and exits 1; same for `--quiet --bogus`.\n- [ ] T015 Verify the quiet line has no leading blank line (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet | head -c 19` prints `Recommended Level: 0`.\n- [ ] T016 Run the existing phase suites (`$S`). Verify: `node tests/test-phase-system.js` and `node tests/test-phase-validation.js` each print `failed=0`.\n- [ ] T017 Reconcile this packet with the shipped behavior (`$P`). Verify: `spec.md` requirement IDs, `plan.md` sections and this file name the same flag and the same line label.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed: one line under `--quiet`, unchanged report without it, both phase suites green\n- [ ] `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh $P --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in `spec.md` section 4\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in `plan.md` section 3\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Baseline report captured in `scratch/baseline-report.txt`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `bash -n .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` exits 0\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No new shellcheck-class warning: every new variable is quoted and declared\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] The new branch follows the existing `case` style and shifts exactly once\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The quiet renderer reads `RECOMMENDED_LEVEL` and `LEVEL_NAME`, not a new label\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] AC-001 through AC-006 in `acceptance-criteria.md` are met with observed evidence\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The new vitest file passes\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases from `spec.md` section 8 are exercised\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error scenarios print to stderr and exit 1\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each actionable finding has a finding class: `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed, or instance-only status proven by grep.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed for changed helpers, policies, schema fields, response fields, docs, and tests.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] Security/path/parser/redaction fixes include adversarial table tests for delimiter, joined-input, outside-root, no-op, and fallback cases.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count are listed before completion is claimed.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Hostile env/global-state variant executed when tests or code read process-wide state.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence is pinned to a fix SHA or explicit diff range, not a moving branch-relative range.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets added; the script reads no credential\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation unchanged: `--quiet` adds no new input value\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] N/A for auth: the script has no authentication or authorization surface\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md` and `tasks.md` name the same flag and the same line label\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The script header OPTIONS block and the `--help` OPTIONS list agree\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] README updated if it documents the script options\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temp files live in `scratch/` only\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` holds only the baseline capture, and it is removed before the packet closes\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 15 | 0/15 |\n| P1 Items | 23 | 0/23 |\n| P2 Items | 9 | 0/9 |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-25\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 is followed: the change is a flag on the existing parser, not an environment variable\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] Both ADRs in `plan.md` carry a status\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Both ADRs list rejected alternatives with a reason\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] N/A for migration: no stored data and no published interface changes\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] NFR-P01 holds: the quiet run finishes within 5 ms of the default run on the same inputs\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P1] N/A for throughput: the script scores one input per invocation\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] N/A for load testing: no service\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] Both timings recorded in `scratch/` with the command used\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure in `plan.md` section 7 was read and the revert path is one commit\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P0] N/A for feature flags: `--quiet` is the opt-in and defaults off\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P1] N/A for monitoring: the script is not a service\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P1] N/A for a runbook: the rollback is a single revert\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] N/A for a deployment runbook: no deploy step\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] N/A for security review: the change alters stdout formatting only\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] No dependency added, so no license changes\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] N/A for OWASP: no network or data surface\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] N/A for data handling: the script stores no data\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md` and `tasks.md` are synchronized on scope and label\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] N/A for API docs: the script is not an API\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] The `--help` text is the user-facing documentation and lists the flag\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] N/A for knowledge transfer: the packet carries the rationale\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| Packet author | Planning | [ ] Approved | |\n| Operator | Implementation | [ ] Approved | |\n| Reviewer | Verification | [ ] Approved | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Paths used below**:\n- `S` = `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`\n- `T` = `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/recommend-level-quiet.vitest.ts`\n- `P` = `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Capture the pre-change report for both reference invocations into `$P/scratch/baseline-report.txt` (`$P/scratch`). Verify: `bash $S --loc 50 --files 2 | wc -l` prints `16` and `bash $S --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural | wc -l` prints `17`.\n- [ ] T002 Read the parser and the output dispatch in `$S`. Verify: `rg -n 'JSON_OUTPUT|output_text|output_json' $S` prints the three decision sites at lines 122, 508, 562 and 770-774.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm no shell consumer parses the report (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'recommend-level\\.sh' . --glob '*.sh' --glob '!node_modules/**'` prints only the script itself.\n- [ ] T004 [P] Record the level label set (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'LEVEL_NAME=' $S` prints `Quick`, `Baseline`, `Verification` and `Full`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T005 Add a `QUIET=false` global beside `JSON_OUTPUT` (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '^QUIET=false' $S` prints one line.\n- [ ] T006 Add the `--quiet` case branch to the argument parser (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n -A 3 -- '--quiet\\)' $S` prints the branch that sets `QUIET=true` and shifts.\n- [ ] T007 Add `output_quiet()` that prints only `Recommended Level: ${RECOMMENDED_LEVEL} (${LEVEL_NAME})` (`$S`). Verify: `bash -n $S` exits 0.\n- [ ] T008 Wire the dispatch so `--quiet` selects the quiet renderer, `--json` keeps precedence and text stays the default (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet | wc -l` prints `1`; `bash $S --loc 50 --files 2 | wc -l` still prints `16`.\n- [ ] T009 Add `--quiet` to the `--help` OPTIONS list and add one quiet example, then update the header OPTIONS block (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --help | rg -c -- '--quiet'` prints `2`.\n- [ ] T010 [P] Create the regression test with cases for none, `--quiet`, `--json`, both flags, `--no-recommend-phases`, and the error paths (`T`). Verify: `npx vitest run tests/recommend-level-quiet.vitest.ts` passes from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T011 Verify the quiet line at every level: 0, 1, 2 and 3 (`$S`). Verify: each of `--loc 10 --files 1`, `--loc 100 --files 5`, `--loc 300 --files 10`, `--loc 900 --files 20 --auth --api --db --architectural` with `--quiet` prints one line that matches `^Recommended Level: [0-3] \\([A-Za-z]+\\)$`.\n- [ ] T012 Verify the default report is byte-identical to the Phase 1 baseline (`$P/scratch`). Verify: `diff` against `baseline-report.txt` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T013 Verify JSON precedence (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --loc 50 --files 2 --json --quiet | node -e 'let s=\"\";process.stdin.on(\"data\",d=>s+=d).on(\"end\",()=>{const j=JSON.parse(s);console.log(j.recommended_level)})'` prints `0`.\n- [ ] T014 Verify error paths keep stdout empty and exit 1 (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet --loc abc` prints the error on stderr, writes nothing to stdout and exits 1; same for `--quiet --bogus`.\n- [ ] T015 Verify the quiet line has no leading blank line (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet | head -c 20` prints `Recommended Level: 0`.\n- [ ] T016 Run the existing phase suites (`$S`). Verify: `node tests/test-phase-system.js` and `node tests/test-phase-validation.js` each print `failed=0`.\n- [ ] T017 Reconcile this packet with the shipped behavior (`$P`). Verify: `spec.md` requirement IDs, `plan.md` sections and this file name the same flag and the same line label.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed: one line under `--quiet`, unchanged report without it, both phase suites green\n- [ ] `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh $P --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in `spec.md` section 4\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in `plan.md` section 3\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Baseline report captured in `scratch/baseline-report.txt`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `bash -n .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` exits 0\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No new shellcheck-class warning: every new variable is quoted and declared\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] The new branch follows the existing `case` style and shifts exactly once\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The quiet renderer reads `RECOMMENDED_LEVEL` and `LEVEL_NAME`, not a new label\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] AC-001 through AC-006 in `acceptance-criteria.md` are met with observed evidence\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The new vitest file passes\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases from `spec.md` section 8 are exercised\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error scenarios print to stderr and exit 1\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each actionable finding has a finding class: `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed, or instance-only status proven by grep.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed for changed helpers, policies, schema fields, response fields, docs, and tests.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] Security/path/parser/redaction fixes include adversarial table tests for delimiter, joined-input, outside-root, no-op, and fallback cases.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count are listed before completion is claimed.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Hostile env/global-state variant executed when tests or code read process-wide state.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence is pinned to a fix SHA or explicit diff range, not a moving branch-relative range.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets added; the script reads no credential\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation unchanged: `--quiet` adds no new input value\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] N/A for auth: the script has no authentication or authorization surface\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md` and `tasks.md` name the same flag and the same line label\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The script header OPTIONS block and the `--help` OPTIONS list agree\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] README updated if it documents the script options\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n#